NNAAMMEE
     mmoopppprroobbee — MOP Probe Utility

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmoopppprroobbee [--33 | --44] [--aaoovv] _i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     mmoopppprroobbee prints the Ethernet address and nodename of DECserver
     100/200/250/300 on the Ethernet connected to _i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e or all known in‐
     terfaces if --aa is given.  If --oo, inhibits all messages but the first from
     a node.  With --vv all MOP/RC SID messages will be shown (e.g., machines
     running DECnet).

     The options are as follows:

     --33      Ignore MOP V3 messages (Ethernet II).

     --44      Ignore MOP V4 messages (Ethernet 802.3).

     --aa      Listen on all the Ethernets attached to the system.  If --aa is
             omitted, an interface must be specified.

     --oo      Print a node just once.

     --vv      Show all nodes sending MOP/RC SID messages.

